  "notes": [
    "Working set (rss) and private committed memory are separate and are never added together.",
    "Windows GetSystemTimes reports machine-wide CPU percent. Process CPU is separately computed from CPU-time delta: 100% means one logical core; dividing by 28 gives machine-equivalent share.",
    "The 2-second sampler can miss short peaks; per-phase CPU can undercount short-lived child processes that exit between samples.",
    "This suite used one fresh launch with default first-paint warmup; the release five-run and interleaved A/B startup evidence are recorded separately. OS file cache was not cleared.",
    "The normal load suite had a sequential health request every 250ms, including the final 30 seconds. The separate fresh-browser idle phase had no HTTP after authentication.",
    "The resource-workspace sample is a single pass over 40 workspaces, not enough to prove or disprove a long-lived cache leak.",
    "No explicit GC was forced in the production server; memory changes include V8 and allocator retention."
  ]
